# conversation-v1: the replies of the chat (DS023 "Conversation layer"). Several reply wires of one situation and part are variants;
# the renderer picks one at random and fills the {{slot}} placeholders from the result packet. Phrasing changes are made here, never in code.

@cv_answer_found_1 reply
  situation answer_found
  part body
  language en
  text "{{answer}}"

@cv_answer_open_1 reply
  situation answer_open
  part body
  language en
  text "{{answer}}"

@cv_near_candidate_1 reply
  situation near_candidate
  part body
  language en
  text "I don't have {{mention}} in my memory. Did you mean {{candidate}}?"

@cv_near_candidate_2 reply
  situation near_candidate
  part body
  language en
  text "I couldn't find {{mention}} in what I know. Perhaps you meant {{candidate}}?"

@cv_near_candidate_described_1 reply
  situation near_candidate_described
  part body
  language en
  text "I don't have {{mention}} in my memory. Did you mean {{candidate}} ({{candidate_description}})?"

@cv_near_candidate_described_2 reply
  situation near_candidate_described
  part body
  language en
  text "I couldn't find {{mention}}, but I know {{candidate}} ({{candidate_description}}). Is that who or what you meant?"

@cv_near_relations_1 reply
  situation near_relations
  part closing
  language en
  text "About {{candidate}} my memory records: {{relations}}."

@cv_near_relations_2 reply
  situation near_relations
  part closing
  language en
  text "I can tell you about {{candidate}} through these relations: {{relations}}."

@cv_offer_topics_1 reply
  situation offer_topics
  part closing
  language en
  text "I know most about {{topics}}, if you want to try one of those."

@cv_offer_topics_2 reply
  situation offer_topics
  part closing
  language en
  text "You could ask me about {{topics}} instead."

@cv_relation_missing_1 reply
  situation relation_missing
  part body
  language en
  text "I understood the question, but my memory has no relation that answers it. You can ask it in other words, or add the knowledge first."

@cv_relation_missing_topics_1 reply
  situation relation_missing_topics
  part body
  language en
  text "I understood the question, but my memory has nothing that answers it. I know most about {{topics}}; ask me about those, or add the knowledge first."

@cv_relation_missing_topics_2 reply
  situation relation_missing_topics
  part body
  language en
  text "That is outside what my memory covers. I can help with {{topics}}, or you can add the knowledge first."

@cv_no_request_1 reply
  situation no_request
  part body
  language en
  text "What would you like to know?"

@cv_no_request_2 reply
  situation no_request
  part body
  language en
  text "How can I help? Ask me a question, or tell me something to remember for this conversation."

@cv_no_request_topics_1 reply
  situation no_request_topics
  part body
  language en
  text "What would you like to know? I can answer questions about {{topics}}, give you a random fact, or tell you what my memory holds."

@cv_no_request_topics_2 reply
  situation no_request_topics
  part body
  language en
  text "Ask me anything about {{topics}}. I can also give you a random fact or describe my memory."

@cv_gibberish_1 reply
  situation gibberish
  part body
  language en
  text "I did not understand the message. Could you rephrase it?"

@cv_gibberish_2 reply
  situation gibberish
  part body
  language en
  text "Sorry, I could not make sense of that. Could you say it in other words?"

@cv_ambiguous_1 reply
  situation ambiguous
  part body
  language en
  text "Your message can be read in more than one way. Which do you mean?"

@cv_ambiguous_readings_1 reply
  situation ambiguous_readings
  part body
  language en
  text "Your message can be read in more than one way. Which do you mean?\n{{readings}}"

@cv_ambiguous_readings_2 reply
  situation ambiguous_readings
  part body
  language en
  text "I see more than one reading here. Which one do you mean?\n{{readings}}"

@cv_courtesy_greeting_1 reply
